 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 *   **Sparse Views:** The method is specifically designed to handle sparse views (e.g., 3 views) where standard NeRF fails due to ambiguity [S2].
-*   **Synthetic Bias:** The diffusion prior is trained on synthetic data (Hypersim). Domain gap between synthetic and real data may affect performance [S2].
-*   **Gradient Noise:** The gradients from the diffusion model may introduce noise if the rendered patches deviate significantly from the training distribution [S2].
+*   **Synthetic Bias:** The diffusion prior is trained on synthetic data (Hypersim), which may cause a domain gap when applied to real-world scenes [S2].
 
